ternal Error ()\nciteturn118view1 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://urengoy-podzemremont.gazprom.ru/press/news/2024/07/494/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\nL0: URL https://urengoy-podzemremont.gazprom.ru/press/news/2024/07/494/ is not accessible via this tool.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAlerts | Intenseye Docs (https://docs.intenseye.com/docs/v2_alerts/index.html)\nciteturn118view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://docs.intenseye.com/docs/v2_alerts/index.html\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 139\nL0: 【0†Skip to main content】\nL1: \nL2:   * 【1†Public API (v2)】\nL3: \nL4:     * 【1†Overview】\nL5:     * 【2†Alerts】\nL6:     * 【3†Alerts with Camera and Facility】\nL7:     * 【4†Alert Rules】\nL8:     * 【5†Cameras】\nL9:     * 【6†Facilities】\nL10:     * 【7†Facility Sections】\nL11:     * 【8†Connectivity】\nL12:     * 【9†Accuracy】\nL13:     * 【10†Ergonomics】\nL14:     * 【11†Tasks】\nL15:     * 【12†Safety Scores】\nL16:     * 【13†Incidents】\nL17: \nL18: [Button: On this page]\nL19: # Alerts\nL20: \nL21: Alerts are the backbone of reporting and it keeps all elements of an alert. Alerts can be queried by string parameters and camera. Alert API works with unix timestamp as the start and end time of the queried alerts and those are required for all type of API calls. So it returns alerts, which created in the given time period only.\nL22: It is recommended to use frequent API calls by keeping the distance between start and end time, because it is easier to manage less alerts at a time. However there is no limitation on start and end times, it is completely up to your scripting structure.\nL23: ### Export alerts based on time interval【14†​】\nL24: \nL25: GET/alerts/export\nL26: \nL27: #### Arguments【15†​】\nL28: ###### Query String Parameters【16†​】\nL29:   * start `Long` required The timestamp where the alerts are happened later\nL30:   * end `Long` required The timestamp where the alerts are happened earlier\nL31:   * facilityId `List[UUID]` optional\nL32:   * cameraId `List[UUID]` optional\nL33:   * format `Enum` optional\nL34:     * CSV (default)\nL35:     * JSON\nL36:     * JSONL\nL37:   * alertType `List[Enum]` optional\nL38:     * HELMET\nL39:     * FACE_MASK\nL40:     * GLOVE...\nL41:   * alertRuleId `List[UUID]` optional\nL42:   * severity `List[Enum]` optional\nL43:     * LOW\nL44:     * MEDIUM\nL45:     * HIGH\nL46:   * observation `Boolean` optional\nL47:   * limit `Int` optional\nL48:   * falsePositive `Boolean` optional\nL49:   * customerFalsePositive `Boolean` optional\nL50:   * intenseyeBookmark `Boolean` optional\nL51:   * bookmark `Boolean` optional\nL52:   * scenarioTemplateType `List[Enum]` optional\nL53:     * PSIF\nL54:     * COMPLIANCE\nL55: #### Returns【17†​】\nL56: \nL57: Returns list of alert objects for given parameters.\nL58: Field  | Type  | Description\nL59: --- | --- | ---\nL60: id  | UUID  | Unique identifier for alert\nL61: name  | Enum  | Alert name ex: GLOVE, HELMET\nL62: localCreatedAt  | DateTime  | Alert creation date\nL63: alertRuleId  | UUID  | Alert rule id\nL64: cameraId  | UUID  | Unique identifier for a camera in which alert is created from\nL65: facilityId  | UUID  | Unique identifier for a facility\nL66: severity  | Enum  | Severity type ex: HIGH, MEDIUM & LOW\nL67: observation  | Boolean  | The field shows that an alert is created for just observation or not\nL68: falsePositive  | Boolean  | The field shows that an alert is marked as false positive by Intenseye team\nL69: customerFalsePositive  | Boolean  | The field shows that an alert is marked as false positive by customers\nL70: intenseyeBookmark  | Boolean  | The field shows that an alert is marked by Intenseye team\nL71: bookmark  | Boolean  | The field shows that an alert is marked by customer\nL72: scenarioTemplateType  | Enum  | Origin scenario template type of the alert. One of `PSIF`, `COMPLIANCE`, or `null` for legacy alerts predating scenario templates\nL73: bannerInfo  | String  | Returns banner in fo on alert image. Ex: Speed limit Motorcycle-30.00kph/31.97kph\nL74: #### P.S: To include NOT reported alerts in falsePositive and customerFalsePositive fields, both parameters must be used in the query parameters as null【18†​】\nL75:   * Csv\nL76:   * Json\nL77:   * Json Lines\nL78: \nL79:     `id,name,localCreatedAt,alertRuleId,cameraId,facilityId,severity,observation,falsePositive,customerFalsePositive,intenseyeBookmark,bookmark,scenarioTemplateType,bannerInfo\nL80:     a68b9378-1a8b-427a-bc6b-a644212a0cb8,HELMET,2022-10-04T20:47:00Z,bd087d4f-13e2-4044-900e-7188b1d4cc0d,d875c064-e8d9-434e-9cee-6996f1549888,3fa85f64-5717-4562-b3fc-2c963f66afa6,LOW,false,true,false,false,PSIF,Speed limit Motorcycle-30.00kph/31.97kph\nL81:     cccd2663-1fa4-40c9-9739-162e474f5c88,GLOVE,2022-10-04T20:51:00Z,bd087d4f-13e2-4044-900e-7188b1d4cc0d,d875c064-e8d9-434e-9cee-6996f1549888,3fa85f64-5717-4562-b3fc-2c963f66afa6,LOW,false,false,false,true,COMPLIANCE,Speed limit Motorcycle-30.00kph/31.97kph\nL82:     `\nL83: \nL84:     `[\nL85:       {\nL86:         \"id\": \"a68b9378-1a8b-427a-bc6b-a644212a0cb8\",\nL87:         \"name\": \"HELMET\",\nL88:         \"localCreatedAt\": \"2022-10-04T20:47:00Z\",\nL89:         \"alertRuleId\": \"bd087d4f-13e2-4044-900e-7188b1d4cc0d\",\nL90:         \"cameraId\": \"d875c064-e8d9-434e-9cee-6996f1549888\",\nL91:         \"facilityId\": \"3fa85f64-5717-4562-b3fc-2c963f66afa6\",\nL92:         \"severity\": \"LOW\",\nL93:         \"observation\": false,\nL94:         \"falsePositive\": true,\nL95:         \"customerFalsePositive\": null,\nL96:         \"intenseyeBookmark\": false,\nL97:         \"bookmark\": false,\nL98:         \"scenarioTemplateType\": \"PSIF\",\nL99:         \"bannerInfo\": \"Speed limit Motorcycle-30.00kph/31.97kph\"\nL100:       },\nL101:       {\nL102:         \"id\": \"cccd2663-1fa4-40c9-9739-162e474f5c88\",\nL103:         \"name\": \"GLOVE\",\nL104:         \"localCreatedAt\": \"2022-10-04T20:51:00Z\",\nL105:         \"alertRuleId\": \"bd087d4f-13e2-4044-900e-7188b1d4cc0d\",\nL106:         \"cameraId\": \"d875c064-e8d9-434e-9cee-6996f1549888\",\nL107:         \"facilityId\": \"3fa85f64-5717-4562-b3fc-2c963f66afa6\",\nL108:         \"severity\": \"LOW\",\nL109:         \"observation\": false,\nL110:         \"falsePositive\": false,\nL111:         \"customerFalsePositive\": null,\nL112:         \"intenseyeBookmark\": false,\nL113:         \"bookmark\": true,\nL114:         \"scenarioTemplateType\": \"COMPLIANCE\",\nL115:         \"bannerInfo\": \"Speed limit Motorcycle-30.00kph/31.97kph\"\nL116:       }\nL117:     ]\nL118:     `\nL119:     `{\"id\":\"a68b9378-1a8b-427a-bc6b-a644212a0cb8\",\"name\":\"HELMET\",\"localCreatedAt\":\"2022-10-04T20:47:00Z\",\"alertRuleId\":\"bd087d4f-13e2-4044-900e-7188b1d4cc0d\",\"cameraId\":\"d875c064-e8d9-434e-9cee-6996f1549888\",\"facilityId\":\"3fa85f64-5717-4562-b3fc-2c963f66afa6\",\"severity\":\"LOW\",\"observation\":false,\"falsePositive\": true, \"customerFalsePositive\": null, \"intenseyeBookmark\": false, \"bookmark\": false,\"scenarioTemplateType\": \"PSIF\",\"bannerInfo\": \"Speed limit Motorcycle-30.00kph/31.97kph\"}\nL120:     {\"id\":\"cccd2663-1fa4-40c9-9739-162e474f5c88\",\"name\":\"GLOVE\",\"localCreatedAt\":\"2022-10-04T20:51:00Z\",\"alertRuleId\":\"bd087d4f-13e2-4044-900e-7188b1d4cc0d\",\"cameraId\":\"d875c064-e8d9-434e-9cee-6996f1549888\",\"facilityId\":\"3fa85f64-5717-4562-b3fc-2c963f66afa6\",\"severity\":\"LOW\",\"observation\":false,\"falsePositive\": false, \"customerFalsePositive\": null, \"intenseyeBookmark\": false, \"bookmark\": true,\"scenarioTemplateType\": \"COMPLIANCE\",\"bannerInfo\": \"Speed limit Motorcycle-30.00kph/31.97kph\"}\nL121:     `\nL122: * * *\nL123: \nL124: 【1†Previous Overview】【3†Next Alerts with Camera and Facility】\nL125: \nL126:   * 【14†Export alerts based on time interval】\nL127: \nL128: Docs\nL129: \nL130:   * 【1†Usage